mctc-lib
------------------------------------------
This library supports reading and writing in more than ten different geometry
formats, including general ASCII formats, like xyz, JSON based formats, like
QCSchema, and program specific formats, for example compatible with Turbomole
or Vasp.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.11-1
  libgfortran5-14.4.0-1
  libjonquil-devel-0.3.2-1bl1
  libjonquil0-0.3.2-1bl1
  libmctc-lib-devel-0.7.0-1bl1
  libmctc-lib0-0.7.0-1bl1
  libtoml-f0-0.5.2-1bl1
  pkg-config-3.0.9-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.10-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  gcc-fortran-14.4.0-1
  libjonquil-devel-0.3.2-1bl1
  libtoml-f-devel-0.5.2-1bl1
  meson-1.10.2-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/grimme-lab/mctc-lib

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/grimme-lab/mctc-lib/archive/refs/tags/v0.7.0.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack mctc-lib-0.7.0-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./mctc-lib-0.7.0-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/mctc-lib-0.7.0-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/mctc-lib-0.7.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libmctc-lib0-0.7.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libmctc-lib-devel-0.7.0-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

